    "stem": "Diya looks at a regular octagon divided into $8$ equal triangular parts that meet at the centre.\n\nWhich claim correctly states the smallest rotation angle about the centre that maps the octagon onto itself, and the order of that rotation?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "The smallest angle is $90^{\\circ}$ and the order is $4$, using only quarter-turns.",
      "B": "The smallest angle is $45^{\\circ}$ and the order is $8$, because $360^{\\circ}\\div 8 = 45^{\\circ}$.",
      "C": "The smallest angle is $30^{\\circ}$ and the order is $12$, as for a clock face.",
      "D": "The smallest angle is $180^{\\circ}$ and the order is $2$, because a half-turn is enough for every regular polygon."
    },
